Add `lastissue import linear`: a built-in subcommand that imports one Linear
project or team into lastissue. Decided in a design grilling session (2026-11-02).

## Command & flow

Interactive on a TTY (via `inquire`), every prompt has a flag; without a TTY a
missing value fails fast (exit 1) naming the flag. The no-prompts rule (§6.2)
stays for the core; importer is the one carve-out.

```
? Linear API key: ********            --api-key / LINEAR_API_KEY
  Authenticated as Ron Jansen @ Acme  (viewer query; workspace = the key's org, not a choice)
? Import by: › Project / Team         --project <name|slug|uuid> | --team <key>
? Project: › [fuzzy list]             completed/cancelled hidden unless --all
? Import into: › New "billing-revamp" / Existing… / No project
                                      --into <project> | --no-project (default: new)
? 30 already imported › Skip / Update --existing skip|update (default skip; asked only if matches)
? Import ~42 issues into …? (y/N)     --yes
```

## Auth
Personal API key only. Never stored on disk. No OAuth.

## Field mapping
| Linear | lastissue |
|---|---|
| title | Subject |
| description (md) | body, 1:1 |
| createdAt | Date (original) |
| creator | From `Name <email>` |
| assignee | To |
| subscribers | Cc |
| state type | triage/backlog→backlog, unstarted→todo, started→in-progress (→in-review if name contains "review"), completed→done, canceled→cancelled, or duplicate + References if duplicateOf is in scope |
| priority 1–4 / 0 | urgent/high/medium/low / none |
| labels | Keywords (lowercased) |
| dueDate | Reply-By |
| parent/blocks/related | X-Parent / X-Blocked-By / X-Related, only if other end in scope |
| comments | messages #2…n, original author/date, threads → In-Reply-To; X-Linear-Comment-Id |
| identifier, url | X-Linear-Id, X-Linear-Url |
| attachments | `[name](url)` links in body |
| history, estimates, cycles, reactions | dropped |

- Team imports: the issue's Linear project name becomes a label.
- `Sender: lastissue-import`. No import events on fresh create.
- Message-IDs are **deterministic** ULIDs: timestamp = createdAt, random part = hash of Linear UUID.

## Re-runs (`--existing`)
Detection: scan the root for X-Linear-Id (message #1 headers only).
- **skip**: leave existing untouched.
- **update**: Linear wins on fields it owns (table above); local-only headers
  (custom X-*, Comments, Sensitivity, Expires) kept. Linear comments appended or
  updated in place (X-Edited); local comments never touched. One
  `X-Issue-Event: update` event listing changes. Issue stays in its current
  folder. Deleted/out-of-scope in Linear → left alone, never deleted locally.

## Fetch/write
- Stream: fetch a page, write a page (atomic per file).
- Relations resolved immediately thanks to deterministic IDs + scope check of the related issue.
- Confirm shows approx count if the API offers one cheaply, else no number.
- stderr progress per page; stdout summary block (X-Imported / X-Updated / X-Skipped) + `--brief` line per touched issue.
- Partial failure: keep what's written; error hints `re-run with --existing skip`.
- 429: honor Retry-After, retry a few times, then fail.

## Dependencies (amend SPEC §7.1, importer only)
`ureq` (blocking HTTP), `serde_json`, `inquire`; dev: `mockito`.

## Testing
- Unit: JSON → Msg mapping for every table row; deterministic ID stability.
- CLI snapshots (assert_cmd + insta) against `mockito`, binary pointed via hidden
  `LINEAR_API_URL`: fresh import, re-run skip, re-run update (assert event),
  500 on page 2 then resume, 429 retry.
- Prompts: manual check only (they fill the same args as flags).
- Optional `#[ignore]` live smoke test when LINEAR_API_KEY is set.

## Also
- Update SPEC.md: new §6 grammar entry, TTY carve-out in §6.2, deps in §7.1, X-Linear-* headers.
- `long_about` with examples per §6.6.

